  "design": {
    "decision": "With [♣]s now short or void, plan to trump [♣] leads and bid the extra trump tricks; Suits teams keep their [♦]s intact.",
    "opponent": "Revealed at Opening; opponents learn the team is short in [♣] and stop leading it.",
    "rationale": "It changes cards from a named side suit, not random cards, so every change adds a trump and removes a side-suit loser, often creating a void. It names [♣] so it never cuts into the [♦] Suits line. It uses a count (Four) rather than every [♣], because the whole-suit version (ca-diamond-become-from-clubs) measured -14.5.",
